# =============================================================================
# Orbital-Drift .gitignore
#
# THE REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC (github.com/ianshank/Orbital-Drift). Constitution
# Principle VII: no credentials in the repo, ever.
#
# Read this before relaxing anything below:
#   gitleaks is a *second* line of defence, not the first. Terraform state
#   routinely embeds plaintext secrets — the CloudNativePG Postgres password,
#   the SeaweedFS S3 access/secret key, the Airflow Fernet key — as ordinary
#   JSON string values. gitleaks' default ruleset keys on recognisable prefixes
#   (AKIA..., ghp_..., -----BEGIN ... KEY-----) and will NOT reliably flag a
#   generated 32-char base64 blob sitting in a state file. Ignoring the file is
#   the real control.
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets and local environment -------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env
# ci/versions.env is a PIN FILE, not an environment file, and `*.env` above
# would swallow it. The negation is anchored to its exact path rather than
# written `!versions.env`, which would also un-ignore a `versions.env` dropped
# anywhere else in the tree.
#
# This is a trap worth naming: any FUTURE `ci/*.env` is silently gitignored by
# the line above AND — because ci/checks.sh derives the working-tree scan's
# exclusions from `git ls-files --others --ignored` — silently dropped from the
# gitleaks walk. It would be invisible to git and to the secret gate at the same
# time. tests/unit/test_ci_contract.py fails if anything under ci/ is ignored.
!/ci/versions.env
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
*.secret
*.secrets

# Private keys and certificates. The pre-commit `detect-private-key` hook is the
# content-side control; these three lines are the path-side one, and they cost
# nothing. Node A's k3s/registry TLS material and any SSH key used to reach it
# land here.
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*

# --- Kubernetes credentials ---------------------------------------------------
kubeconfig
kubeconfig*
*.kubeconfig
.kube/
k3s.yaml

# --- Terraform ----------------------------------------------------------------
# State first: it is the highest-value leak in this repo (see header).
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup
.terraform/
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
crash.log
crash.*.log
terraform.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# Variable files carry operator-specific values (${NODE_A_LAN_IP}, GPU UUIDs —
# D-03/D-10). Examples are committed; real ones never are.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!*.tfvars.example
!*.tfvars.json.example

# NOT ignored, deliberately: .terraform.lock.hcl
# It is a provider *pin* artifact and Constitution IV requires it committed.
# Do not add it here.

# --- Helm ---------------------------------------------------------------------
charts/*.tgz
infra/helm-values/**/*.local.yaml
infra/helm-values/**/*.secret.yaml

# --- Python -------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
sdist/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

# Virtualenvs
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
env/
.python-version

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
*.cover
.hypothesis/

# --- ML / data artefacts ------------------------------------------------------
# Datasets and models are addressed by lakeFS commit and MLflow run ID
# (Constitution IV), never by a file in git.
mlruns/
mlartifacts/
data/raw/
data/interim/
data/processed/
*.tif
*.tiff
*.jp2
*.nc
*.parquet
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.onnx

# --- Editors / OS -------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Local scratch ------------------------------------------------------------
scratch/
tmp/
.local/

# Claude Code agent worktrees. The harness checks out one working tree per
# concurrent subagent dispatch under here (isolation: "worktree"); each is a
# full nested git checkout, not repository content, and must never be staged.
.claude/worktrees/
